Z||000000||formula2||07-15-2001||11:49 AM||||I'm not a mechanic but i can check an air filter . But where is it??<BR>I just found the engine..Joke.........<P>I have to change a light in the back where it is written Pontiac.Where is the socket????<P>Pontiac Grand Prix GT 1997  <BR>Pontiac Fiero GT 1986<BR>GMC Savana 2000||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||07-15-2001||12:13 PM||||Open (rear) hood.  I know you just figured out which end that is   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>On the ledge just aft of the trunk compartment, just above the taillights, you will see a row of black plastic, rectangular plugs.  Gently pry them off with a flat screwdriver, and you will find a Phillips-head screw underneath each one.<P>So, loosen and remove the Phillips-head screws, and the taillight assemblies fall out into your waiting hands.  From that point, it should be obvious what to do.<P>If not, post again, and we'll be glad to help.<P>BTW, welcome to the Forum   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  And in case you weren't kidding about the air filter, it's inside the big can underneath the (black) vent on the LHS of hood, just aft of the rear window.  This one breathes from the inside, so the inside of the filter gets dirty, instead of the outside.  You probably knew all that, but oh, well.        <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-15-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||btoth||07-15-2001||12:18 PM||||The air filter is under the driver-side vent.||||reg||7
